# The commit of qoryai/integrations that the integration contract
# (contracts/integration/v1) and the data descriptions in this repository are copied
# from, byte for byte.
# `test/apiary/contract_copies_test.exs` checks each copy against
# `test/fixtures/contract-copies.sha256`, the SHA-256 of each file at this commit.
#
# To vendor another commit: copy every file again from integrations at that commit, write
# the commit on the last line of this file and in test/fixtures/contract/integration/v1/
# .contract-ref, and set `@ref` in the test. Then run this command at the repository's
# root to write the manifest again:
#
#   find priv/contract/integration test/fixtures/contract/integration/v1 \
#       test/fixtures/integration-contract -type f ! -name .contract-ref |
#     LC_ALL=C sort | xargs shasum -a 256 > test/fixtures/contract-copies.sha256
#
# The command hashes the copies here, so it is right only after the copy.
#
# contracts/integration/v1 is copied to three places:
# - its schemas and README.md, to test/fixtures/contract/integration/v1/,
# - connect-return.schema.json and setup-pass.schema.json, to
#   test/fixtures/integration-contract/schema/,
# - its fixtures/ folder, to test/fixtures/integration-contract/: the description
#   fixtures, accepted, refused under invalid/, refused by a reader under
#   refused-by-reader/, and the documents that only a closed copy of a schema refuses
#   under closed/; and under adapter/ the fixtures of each request, answer and report
#   of the adapter contract.
#
# description.schema.json, definitions.schema.json, changes.schema.json (which
# Apiary.Adapters.ChangeRequest checks an entry against), changes-submitted.schema.json
# and changes-failed.schema.json (which Apiary.Adapters.ChangeReport checks a report
# against) are copied to priv/contract/integration/ too, and the data descriptions of
# model providers, descriptions/*.json at the repository's root, to
# priv/contract/integration/descriptions/.
#
# priv/contract/integration/ has no `.contract-ref`: this file covers it. The run
# contract is copied from this commit too: see test/fixtures/contract/run/v1/
# .contract-ref. The explore, diagnostics and provisioner contracts and the run
# contract's documents.schema.json in lib/apiary/stacks/ are copied from other
# integrations commits: see `.contract-ref` in test/fixtures/contract/<contract>/v1/
# and lib/apiary/stacks/.
#
# Qory Apiary checks the bounds of a description: the 256 KiB of a fetched
# description.json when it is fetched, and every bound, those 256 KiB included, in
# Apiary.Integrations.Description.parse/1, which an adapter's start-up calls with the
# description's value from the body of the start-up. The schema checks the shape of each
# `links` entry. Qory Apiary does not check that each system is listed once or that the
# host of a template is its system, which integrations' `contracts.CheckLinks` checks.
